<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyspaosines</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 124 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hyspaosines was the founder of the kingdom of Characene at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>. A Seleucid governor of Iranian origin, he restored the flooded city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charax-spasinou">Charax Spasinou</a>, declared independence as Seleucid power collapsed around 141 BCE, and briefly held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in 127 BCE during the wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a>. He died in 124 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hyspaosines.jpg" alt="Hyspaosines" width="320" height="150" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Hyspaosines,_minted_at_Charax_Spasinu_in_126-5_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
